===Adjective===
{{en-adj}} {{tlb|en|possessional}}

# [[absent|Absent]] in [[mind]]; often [[preoccupied]]; [[forgetful]] or [[careless]] due to [[distraction]]; easily [[distract]]ed. {{defdate|First attested in the mid 19<sup>th</sup> century.}}<ref name=SOED>{{R:SOED5|page=9}}</ref>
#: ''It took the '''absent-minded''' man twenty minutes to find his glasses on top of his head.''
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1900|author=w:Kenneth Grahame|title={{w|The Golden Age (Grahame)|The Golden Age}}|page=110|passage=His figure was bent in apologetic protest. "I ask a thousand pardons, sir," he said; "I am really so very '''absent-minded'''."}}

